<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Abstractions\Harbor.Abstractions.csproj"/>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Ui.Framework\Harbor.Ui.Framework.csproj"/>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Terminal.Abstractions\Harbor.Terminal.Abstractions.csproj"/>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Tui.AnsiPlain\Harbor.Tui.AnsiPlain.csproj"/>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Harbor.Hosting\Harbor.Hosting.csproj"/>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      §ARCH-003 sweep (#910): `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection` is
      gone. No IServiceCollection, ServiceDescriptor, Add* or
      BuildServiceProvider appears anywhere in this project; the only occurrence
      of the token was the PackageReference line itself.

      ASYMMETRY WITH THE OTHER #910 REFERENCE, and the reason the two are in
      separate commits: this removal is COSMETIC. Resolved against the net10.0
      dependency groups of the real nuspecs, after deleting this line the
      package still reaches this project by three routes:

        Microsoft.Extensions.Logging      (src/Harbor.Application,
                                         src/Harbor.Registries,
                                         src/Harbor.Ui.Framework.Services,
                                         src/Harbor.Ui.Framework.Sessions)
        Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting       (contrib/tui/Harbor.Tui.Termina)
        RazorConsole.Core                  (contrib/tui/Harbor.Tui.RazorConsole)

      So the assembly stays in the compile closure and nothing about the build
      or the shipped binary changes. The line was still false and is still
      worth deleting, but deleting it is not evidence of anything — in
      particular it is not an AOT win: Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
      10.0.10 ships IsAotCompatible metadata, and no workflow in
      .github/workflows/ publishes with HarborWithAot=true anyway, so "this
      package was an AOT liability" is not a claim anything here can falsify.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
